diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ea556e0..3f6fc56 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -33,6 +33,12 @@ An animated urban scene showing pedestrians, cars, buses, bicycles, and taxis mo
 
 Real-time public transport overlay using the Västtrafik API. Displays live positions of buses, trams, trains, and ferries with smooth interpolated movement and trailing paths. Vehicle types are colour-coded and can be filtered by transport mode.
 
+### 🚶 Slow Walkers: Time Lost
+
+How many minutes slow walkers (Västtrafik's "slow" 4.235 km/h, typical of elderly passengers) lose when they miss a public-transport connection that medium-speed walkers (4.8 km/h) make. Computed with r5py on the Västtrafik GTFS timetable for weekday departures between 06:00 and 22:00, and exported to `media/slow-walkers/slow-walkers.geojson` by the separate `slow_walkers` project (`export_mr_layer.py`).
+
+Cells are 50 m around Chalmers (the table's calibrated view) and 200 m across the rest of Gothenburg, so the layer works on the campus model and zoomed out to the whole city. The controller has a time-of-day slider (or the all-day average), a play button that steps through the day, and a Chalmers / Gothenburg view switch. Cells grow in on activation, as in the original animation.
+
 ### 🌬️ CFD Wind Simulation
 
 Real-time Lattice Boltzmann computational fluid dynamics simulation showing wind flow patterns around buildings. The simulation computes fluid dynamics on the fly and visualises velocity fields with colour-coded flow lines. Wind audio plays whilst the simulation is active.
